              "text": "かんじゃ (kanja) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are kan, \"to suffer, illness\" (Middle Chinese hwaenH) and ja, \"person\" (tsyaeX) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription). The second is voiced from sha to ja."
            }
